  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///README.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "# Privacy Gateway \342\200\224 Production-Oriented VPN & Privacy Platform\n\n> **Phase 1 Foundation: Monorepo Setup, Docker Orchestration, PostgreSQL Migration System & Health Services**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Overview\n\nPrivacy Gateway is a WireGuard-based VPN service combined with a privacy-intelligence platform.\n\nThis repository represents the **Phase 1 Foundation** established according to the approved **Phase 0.1 Master Architecture**:\n- Strict separation between the **Cryptographic WireGuard Data Plane** (zero browsing logs) and the **Control Plane** (Node/Express API + PostgreSQL).\n- Standard monorepo layout (`apps/api`, `apps/web`, `packages/shared-types`, `infrastructure/migrations`).\n- Hardened Docker Compose environment with non-root containers (`UID 10001`), read-only root filesystems, dropped Linux capabilities (`cap_drop: ALL`), and isolated internal networking.\n- Relational PostgreSQL 16 schema with 10 core tables, foreign key constraints, UUID generation, and crypto extensions.\n- Structured JSON logging with zero PII retention.\n- Health checking endpoints (`/health`, `/health/live`, `/health/ready`) with latency metrics and live database/redis probing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Monorepo Structure\n\n```\nprivacy-gateway/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example                       # Root environment variable template\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .gitignore                         # Build and secret ignore rules\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docker-compose.yml                 # Local Docker orchestration (Postgres, Redis, API)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json                       # Root workspace orchestrator\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.base.json                 # Shared TypeScript base configuration\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.json                      # Workspace path aliases\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 apps/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/                           # Express TypeScript backend service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/                # Zod env schema, PostgreSQL pool, Redis client\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 controllers/           # Health & System info controllers\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middleware/            # Security headers, zero-PII logger, error handler\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/                # Express router definitions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.ts                 # Express application\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts              # API server lifecycle & graceful shutdown\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 tests/                     # Automated unit and integration tests\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 web/                           # React 19 + Tailwind CSS operations dashboard\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                # Live Phase 1 health & architecture dashboard\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docker/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Dockerfile                 # Multi-stage non-root container (UID 10001)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 postgres/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 init-db.sh                 # Database initialization hooks\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 infrastructure/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 migrations/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 001_initial_schema.sql     # Initial 10-table PostgreSQL DDL\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 runner.ts                  # Transactional migration engine\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 packages/\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 shared-types/                  # Shared TypeScript interfaces & DTOs\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n            \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts                 # API contracts, health & telemetry DTOs\n            \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 db.ts                  # Database table entity interfaces\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Quickstart & Local Setup\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Node.js 20+ / 22+\n- Docker & Docker Compose\n\n### Step 1: Clone and Configure Environment\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n```\n\n### Step 2: Start with Docker Compose (Recommended)\n```bash\ndocker-compose up -d --build\n```\nThis boots:\n1. `pg_database` (PostgreSQL 16 on `localhost:5432` with `001_initial_schema.sql` pre-loaded)\n2. `pg_redis` (Redis 7 on `localhost:6379`)\n3. `pg_api` (Privacy Gateway API on `http://localhost:3000`)\n\n### Step 3: Run Standalone Development (Host Mode)\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\nUnified development server boots on `http://localhost:3000` hosting both the Express API routes and the Vite web dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Database Migrations\n\nThe transactional migration engine inspects `_migrations` and applies pending `.sql` files within discrete transactions:\n\n```bash\nnpm run migrate\n```\n\n### Core Tables Created (Phase 1):\n1. `users` \342\200\224 Primary account records and configurable retention limits (1\342\200\223365 days).\n2. `authentication_accounts` \342\200\224 OIDC / Google OAuth linked accounts.\n3. `user_sessions` \342\200\224 Refresh token hashes and anonymized client IP prefixes.\n4. `devices` \342\200\224 Registered desktop and mobile client instances.\n5. `vpn_servers` \342\200\224 WireGuard infrastructure node endpoints and CIDRs.\n6. `wireguard_peers` \342\200\224 Curve25519 public keys and allocated VPN IPs.\n7. `subscriptions` \342\200\224 Plan tiers (Free, Premium, Business) and device quotas.\n8. `privacy_scans` \342\200\224 Deterministic 4-pillar privacy scores and explanations.\n9. `privacy_events` \342\200\224 Configurable retention stream for tracker and leak events.\n10. `audit_logs` \342\200\224 Immutable security event log.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Health Endpoints & Live Probing\n\n| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `/health` | `GET` | Full diagnostic probe measuring PostgreSQL & Redis latency, memory RSS/heap, and uptime. |\n| `/health/live` | `GET` | Kubernetes / Docker liveness probe verifying event loop responsiveness. |\n| `/health/ready` | `GET` | Readiness probe confirming PostgreSQL connectivity before accepting traffic. |\n| `/api/v1/system/info` | `GET` | System architecture parameters, security boundaries, and migration status. |\n| `/api/v1/system/migrations` | `GET` | List of defined and applied database migrations. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Running Automated Tests\n\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\nRuns automated unit and integration tests verifying environment validation, schema parsing, and health routes.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Upcoming Phases (Per Approved Roadmap)\n\n- **Phase 2**: OpenID Connect & Google OAuth 2.0 PKCE Authentication (Web + Desktop RFC 8252 Loopback).\n- **Phase 3**: Real WireGuard Server Node Controller (Linux Netlink Daemon + nftables NAT).\n- **Phase 4**: Core REST API & Real-time WebSocket Ingestion Bus.\n- **Phase 5**: Desktop Client Core (Tauri / Rust Engine).\n- **Phase 6**: Browser Privacy Extension (Manifest V3 Tracker Blocker).\n- **Phase 7**: Deterministic Privacy Scoring Engine & Synthetic DNS/WebRTC Probers.\n"
    }
