  planner_response {
    response: "# PRIVACY GATEWAY \342\200\224 PHASE 1 IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Was Implemented\n\nThe **Phase 1 Foundation** for Privacy Gateway has been established:\n\n- **Monorepo Architecture**: Cleanly partitioned workspace organized into `apps/api`, `apps/web`, `packages/shared-types`, and `infrastructure/migrations`.\n- **Backend Service (`apps/api`)**: Production-ready Express TypeScript backend with strict Zod environment variable parsing, Helmet security headers, CORS protection, structured JSON logging with zero PII retention, and graceful connection draining.\n- **Health Check & Diagnostic Probing**: Live endpoints (`/health`, `/health/live`, `/health/ready`, `/api/v1/system/info`, `/api/v1/system/migrations`) measuring runtime metrics, memory RSS/heap allocations, and database/Redis connectivity.\n- **Relational PostgreSQL 16 Schema**: Migration `001_initial_schema.sql` defining the 10 core tables with foreign keys, checks, UUID generation, crypto extensions, and performance indices.\n- **Transactional Migration Engine (`infrastructure/migrations/runner.ts`)**: Applies SQL migrations within atomic transactions and tracks applied states in `_migrations`.\n- **Hardened Docker Orchestration (`docker-compose.yml`, `docker/api/Dockerfile`)**: Multi-stage non-root container (`UID 10001:10001`), read-only root filesystems, dropped capabilities (`cap_drop: ALL`), and network isolation.\n- **Web Operations Dashboard (`apps/web`)**: Interactive real-time dashboard displaying active service health, memory metrics, database schema definitions, security enclaves, and an interactive live endpoint prober.\n- **Automated Test Suite**: Unit and integration tests for environment parsing and application bootstrap using native `node:test`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files Changed & Created\n\n```\nprivacy-gateway/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example                               # Environment template with Postgres, Redis & CORS config\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docker-compose.yml                         # Hardened multi-container orchestration\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json                               # Workspace scripts (dev, build, test, migrate)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md                                  # Complete Phase 1 setup and operation guide\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.base.json                         # Base compiler configuration\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.json                              # Workspace path aliases (@shared/*, @apps/*)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                                  # Unified entry point (Express API + Vite Dev Middleware)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 apps/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.ts                         # Express application factory & middleware chain\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                      # Standalone API server with graceful shutdown\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.ts                     # Zod environment schema & validation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database.ts                # PostgreSQL connection pool with health probes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 redis.ts                   # Redis client manager with health probes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 controllers/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 health.controller.ts       # /health, /health/live, /health/ready\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 system.controller.ts       # /api/v1/system/info, /api/v1/system/migrations\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middleware/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 error.middleware.ts        # Standardized error response envelope\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 logging.middleware.ts      # Structured JSON request logger (Zero PII)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 security.middleware.ts     # Helmet headers & CORS policy\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 health.routes.ts\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 system.routes.ts\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 tests/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.test.ts                    # Automated environment validation test\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 health.test.ts                 # Automated health controller test\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 web/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                        # Live Phase 1 telemetry & architecture UI\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docker/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Dockerfile                         # Multi-stage non-root container (UID 10001)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 infrastructure/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 migrations/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 001_initial_schema.sql             # 10 core relational PostgreSQL tables\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 runner.ts                          # Transactional migration engine\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 packages/\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 shared-types/\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n            \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts\n            \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts                         # API DTO contracts & health response types\n            \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 db.ts                          # PostgreSQL entity models\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Database Changes (PostgreSQL Schema)\n\nDefined and scripted in `infrastructure/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql`:\n\n1. `_migrations` \342\200\224 Transactional migration tracking table with SHA-256 checksums.\n2. `users` \342\200\224 Unique UUIDs, email identities, roles (`user`, `admin`, `auditor`), and configurable retention (1\342\200\223365 days).\n3. `authentication_accounts` \342\200\224 OIDC / OAuth provider bindings (`provider`, `provider_subject_id`).\n4. `user_sessions` \342\200\224 Refresh token CSPRNG hashes and anonymized client IP prefixes.\n5. `devices` \342\200\224 Registered client devices, platform types, and versioning.\n6. `vpn_servers` \342\200\224 WireGuard infrastructure nodes, public endpoints, and CIDR subnets.\n7. `wireguard_peers` \342\200\224 Curve25519 public keys, assigned VIPs, and monotonic byte counters.\n8. `subscriptions` \342\200\224 Plan tiers (`free`, `premium`, `business`), device quotas, and billing status.\n9. `privacy_scans` \342\200\224 Deterministic 4-pillar privacy scores and structured explanations.\n10. `privacy_events` \342\200\224 Configurable retention stream for tracker and leak events.\n11. `audit_logs` \342\200\224 Immutable security event audit log.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security & Privilege Implications\n\n- **Separation of Concerns**: The VPN data plane does not touch the database, preserving the Zero Browsing Logs guarantee at the architectural level.\n- **Zero PII Logging**: The HTTP logging middleware strips all query parameters and request bodies, recording only HTTP method, sanitized path, status code, latency, and request ID.\n- **Docker Hardening**: API container runs as unprivileged user `10001:10001`, drops all Linux capabilities (`cap_drop: ALL`), enforces `read_only: true` on the root filesystem, and isolates the database on `pg-internal-net`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. How to Run & Test\n\n### Run Local Development Server:\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\nUnified server binds to `http://0.0.0.0:3000`, serving both the API routes (`/health`, `/api/v1/*`) and the live React dashboard.\n\n### Run Automated Unit & Integration Tests:\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\n### Run Database Migrations:\n```bash\nnpm run migrate\n```\n\n### Boot with Docker Compose:\n```bash\ndocker-compose up -d --build\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. What Is Explicitly NOT Implemented Yet (Deferred to Later Phases)\n\n- \342\235\214 Google OAuth / OIDC PKCE authentication logic (Phase 2)\n- \342\235\214 WireGuard server netlink daemon & kernel peer control (Phase 3)\n- \342\235\214 Tauri desktop client (Phase 5)\n- \342\235\214 Browser extension (Phase 6)\n- \342\235\214 Privacy scoring computation & tracker classification (Phase 7)\n- \342\235\214 Synthetic DNS/WebRTC leak probers (Phase 7)\n- \342\235\214 Multi-region production infrastructure & billing integration (Phases 12+)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Next Recommended Phase\n\n**Phase 2: Authentication & Google OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect Engine (PKCE Hardened for Web & Desktop RFC 8252 Loopback)**"
    modified_response: "# PRIVACY GATEWAY \342\200\224 PHASE 1 IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Was Implemented\n\nThe **Phase 1 Foundation** for Privacy Gateway has been established:\n\n- **Monorepo Architecture**: Cleanly partitioned workspace organized into `apps/api`, `apps/web`, `packages/shared-types`, and `infrastructure/migrations`.\n- **Backend Service (`apps/api`)**: Production-ready Express TypeScript backend with strict Zod environment variable parsing, Helmet security headers, CORS protection, structured JSON logging with zero PII retention, and graceful connection draining.\n- **Health Check & Diagnostic Probing**: Live endpoints (`/health`, `/health/live`, `/health/ready`, `/api/v1/system/info`, `/api/v1/system/migrations`) measuring runtime metrics, memory RSS/heap allocations, and database/Redis connectivity.\n- **Relational PostgreSQL 16 Schema**: Migration `001_initial_schema.sql` defining the 10 core tables with foreign keys, checks, UUID generation, crypto extensions, and performance indices.\n- **Transactional Migration Engine (`infrastructure/migrations/runner.ts`)**: Applies SQL migrations within atomic transactions and tracks applied states in `_migrations`.\n- **Hardened Docker Orchestration (`docker-compose.yml`, `docker/api/Dockerfile`)**: Multi-stage non-root container (`UID 10001:10001`), read-only root filesystems, dropped capabilities (`cap_drop: ALL`), and network isolation.\n- **Web Operations Dashboard (`apps/web`)**: Interactive real-time dashboard displaying active service health, memory metrics, database schema definitions, security enclaves, and an interactive live endpoint prober.\n- **Automated Test Suite**: Unit and integration tests for environment parsing and application bootstrap using native `node:test`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files Changed & Created\n\n```\nprivacy-gateway/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example                               # Environment template with Postgres, Redis & CORS config\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docker-compose.yml                         # Hardened multi-container orchestration\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json                               # Workspace scripts (dev, build, test, migrate)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md                                  # Complete Phase 1 setup and operation guide\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.base.json                         # Base compiler configuration\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.json                              # Workspace path aliases (@shared/*, @apps/*)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                                  # Unified entry point (Express API + Vite Dev Middleware)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 apps/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.ts                         # Express application factory & middleware chain\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                      # Standalone API server with graceful shutdown\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.ts                     # Zod environment schema & validation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database.ts                # PostgreSQL connection pool with health probes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 redis.ts                   # Redis client manager with health probes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 controllers/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 health.controller.ts       # /health, /health/live, /health/ready\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 system.controller.ts       # /api/v1/system/info, /api/v1/system/migrations\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middleware/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 error.middleware.ts        # Standardized error response envelope\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 logging.middleware.ts      # Structured JSON request logger (Zero PII)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 security.middleware.ts     # Helmet headers & CORS policy\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 health.routes.ts\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 system.routes.ts\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 tests/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.test.ts                    # Automated environment validation test\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 health.test.ts                 # Automated health controller test\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 web/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                        # Live Phase 1 telemetry & architecture UI\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docker/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Dockerfile                         # Multi-stage non-root container (UID 10001)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 infrastructure/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 migrations/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 001_initial_schema.sql             # 10 core relational PostgreSQL tables\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 runner.ts                          # Transactional migration engine\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 packages/\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 shared-types/\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n            \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts\n            \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts                         # API DTO contracts & health response types\n            \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 db.ts                          # PostgreSQL entity models\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Database Changes (PostgreSQL Schema)\n\nDefined and scripted in `infrastructure/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql`:\n\n1. `_migrations` \342\200\224 Transactional migration tracking table with SHA-256 checksums.\n2. `users` \342\200\224 Unique UUIDs, email identities, roles (`user`, `admin`, `auditor`), and configurable retention (1\342\200\223365 days).\n3. `authentication_accounts` \342\200\224 OIDC / OAuth provider bindings (`provider`, `provider_subject_id`).\n4. `user_sessions` \342\200\224 Refresh token CSPRNG hashes and anonymized client IP prefixes.\n5. `devices` \342\200\224 Registered client devices, platform types, and versioning.\n6. `vpn_servers` \342\200\224 WireGuard infrastructure nodes, public endpoints, and CIDR subnets.\n7. `wireguard_peers` \342\200\224 Curve25519 public keys, assigned VIPs, and monotonic byte counters.\n8. `subscriptions` \342\200\224 Plan tiers (`free`, `premium`, `business`), device quotas, and billing status.\n9. `privacy_scans` \342\200\224 Deterministic 4-pillar privacy scores and structured explanations.\n10. `privacy_events` \342\200\224 Configurable retention stream for tracker and leak events.\n11. `audit_logs` \342\200\224 Immutable security event audit log.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security & Privilege Implications\n\n- **Separation of Concerns**: The VPN data plane does not touch the database, preserving the Zero Browsing Logs guarantee at the architectural level.\n- **Zero PII Logging**: The HTTP logging middleware strips all query parameters and request bodies, recording only HTTP method, sanitized path, status code, latency, and request ID.\n- **Docker Hardening**: API container runs as unprivileged user `10001:10001`, drops all Linux capabilities (`cap_drop: ALL`), enforces `read_only: true` on the root filesystem, and isolates the database on `pg-internal-net`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. How to Run & Test\n\n### Run Local Development Server:\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\nUnified server binds to `http://0.0.0.0:3000`, serving both the API routes (`/health`, `/api/v1/*`) and the live React dashboard.\n\n### Run Automated Unit & Integration Tests:\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\n### Run Database Migrations:\n```bash\nnpm run migrate\n```\n\n### Boot with Docker Compose:\n```bash\ndocker-compose up -d --build\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. What Is Explicitly NOT Implemented Yet (Deferred to Later Phases)\n\n- \342\235\214 Google OAuth / OIDC PKCE authentication logic (Phase 2)\n- \342\235\214 WireGuard server netlink daemon & kernel peer control (Phase 3)\n- \342\235\214 Tauri desktop client (Phase 5)\n- \342\235\214 Browser extension (Phase 6)\n- \342\235\214 Privacy scoring computation & tracker classification (Phase 7)\n- \342\235\214 Synthetic DNS/WebRTC leak probers (Phase 7)\n- \342\235\214 Multi-region production infrastructure & billing integration (Phases 12+)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Next Recommended Phase\n\n**Phase 2: Authentication & Google OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect Engine (PKCE Hardened for Web & Desktop RFC 8252 Loopback)**"
