token AND `role === \'admin\'`. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Security Implementations Completed\n\n1. **CSRF Protection on `/auth/refresh` and All State Mutations**:\n   - Implemented Double-Submit Cookie CSRF middleware (`apps/api/src/middleware/csrf.middleware.ts`) enforcing constant-time string comparison (`crypto.timingSafeEqual`).\n   - Covered `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh`, `POST /api/v1/auth/logout`, and `DELETE /api/v1/auth/sessions/:id`.\n2. **Strict Atomic Refresh Token Rotation & Zero Plaintext Secrets**:\n   - Refresh tokens are stored exclusively as `SHA-256(raw_token)` hashes.\n   - Rotated tokens are recorded in `session_token_history`. If a rotated token is submitted, the server flags a replay attack and revokes all sessions in that `family_id`.\n3. **Removal of `COOKIE_SECRET`**:\n   - Cleanly eliminated `COOKIE_SECRET` from environment variables, configuration files, and code.\n4. **RS256 Asymmetric Key Lifecycle**:\n   - Production requires explicit `JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM` and `JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM`.\n   - Development generates an ephemeral 2048-bit RSA keypair at startup with explicit logging.\n5. **Native Desktop OAuth Contract (RFC 8252)**:\n   - Implemented `POST /api/v1/auth/desktop/google/exchange` with loopback redirect URI validation for the Phase 5 Tauri client.\n6. **Database Migration 002**:\n   - Created `infrastructure/migrations/002_auth_token_families.sql` introducing `session_token_history`, adding `family_id`, and dropping `client_ip_anonymized` for total IP minimization.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Actual Automated Test Suite Results\n\nRan test runner: `npm test` (`tsx --test apps/api/tests/*.test.ts`)\n\n```\nTAP version 13\n# Subtest: RS256 JWT Token Service Tests\n    # Subtest: should generate and verify valid RS256 access tokens\n    ok 1 - should generate and verify valid RS256 access tokens\n    # Subtest: should generate high entropy CSPRNG refresh tokens and correct SHA-256 hashes\n    ok 2 - should generate high entropy CSPRNG refresh tokens and c