    thinking: "**Analyzing the Setup**\n\nI\'m currently digging into the application\'s configuration, focusing on the `.env.example` file and `env.ts`. It seems the default Google OAuth client ID and secret are set to placeholder values, which is good. I need to determine how these variables are used in the application flow.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Redirect Issues**\n\nI\'ve discovered the default Google OAuth setup uses placeholder client secrets and a redirect URI set to localhost. When I triggered the Google OAuth flow, the backend correctly redirected to Google\'s authorization endpoint, but the placeholder client ID caused immediate rejection, or iframe blockage of the redirect. Errors from Google, and the `handleGoogleCallback` function are routed to the index page. This suggests the authentication flow is fundamentally flawed.\n\n\n**Refining Cookie Handling**\n\nI\'ve been examining the cookie attributes, specifically within the `setAuthCookies` function. The current configuration attempts to handle different environments (production, iframe, localhost). However, I\'ve noticed inconsistencies in how browsers treat cookies with `SameSite=Lax` or without `Secure=true` in iframe contexts.  I need to refine the cookie settings to be more robust for cross-origin scenarios.\n\n\n**Optimizing Redirect Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the redirect URI construction within `startGoogleAuth`. It\'s crucial this is constructed dynamically using `req`, `APP_URL`, or `origin` to accommodate both Cloud Run preview URLs and local development. I must handle both the `http://localhost:3000` and the Cloud Run domain variants effectively.\n\nI also need to improve the popup or direct flow handling. Specifically, inside an iframe or browser popup, Google blocks the flow with `X-Frame-Options: DENY`. I am now focusing on the need to utilize `GET /api/v1/auth/google/start?mode=json` or `POST /api/v1/auth/` in these contexts.\n\n\n"
