    thinking: "**Analyzing Potential Failures**\n\nI\'m now investigating potential failure points related to database connections. I\'m focusing on scenarios where PostgreSQL or Redis are unavailable or if a database connection fails. I\'m currently examining `apps/api/src/services/auth.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/config/database.ts` to identify how these failures are currently handled.\n\n\n**Investigating In-Memory Fallbacks**\n\nI\'m now thinking about in-memory fallbacks for development. If PostgreSQL or Redis are unavailable, I\'ll implement in-memory alternatives. This will ensure full application functionality in a standalone Node environment, including user and session management. I\'ll need to handle transactions gracefully and ensure seamless transitions to real databases when available. I\'m focusing on the configuration aspect. I also will begin to check Google related configuration items, starting with `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`.\n\n\n**Configuring Google OAuth**\n\nI\'ve just added several Google OAuth configurations. I have the `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` loaded from the environment. `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` is now dynamically resolved, which supports both local and cloud environments. For Google Cloud OAuth, I\'ll display the exact callback URI and Javascript origins in the UI for ease of use. I\'m also planning to incorporate a diagnostic checklist to clarify the consent screen settings.\n\n\n**Implementing OAuth Safeguards**\n\nI\'m now implementing safeguards related to OAuth flows and I am focusing on handling potential errors from Google\'s callback. Specifically, I\'m ensuring OAuth state integrity with Redis, using `GETDEL` for atomic consumption or a fallback, and returning clear 400 errors for invalid or expired states. I am implementing clean error dialogs in the UI for Google authentication cancellations or rejections. For the token exchange, I\'m sending specific parameters and sanitizing error responses like `invalid_grant` to provide clearer feedback. I\'ll be also validating OIDC with JWKS and `RS256` signature for security.\n\n\n"
