    thinking: "**Examining Google Login**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `handleStartGoogleLogin` function within `src/App.tsx`, specifically lines 116-118. The function redirects to `/api/v1/auth/google/start`. My primary goal is understanding how this flow behaves within the AI Studio iframe environment on `ais-dev-*.run.app` for Google login functionality. The next step is navigating the function and the behavior within the iframe.\n\n\n**Analyzing Google Redirect Flow**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root cause of the Google login failure within the iframe. Direct redirection to Google\'s OAuth URL is blocked due to `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and CSP. However, now I\'m evaluating the popup-based OAuth approach. The logic involves opening a popup window for Google authorization. Upon authentication, Google redirects back to `/api/v1/auth/google/callback`, which sets cookies for iframe compatibility before sending a message via `postMessage`.\n\n\n**Refining Google Authentication Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how `/api/v1/auth/google/start` handles requests. If it\'s a standard browser navigation, it\'s a redirect, but for JSON requests, it returns a success object with a URL. Also, I\'ve outlined error handling. For canceled logins, it\'ll display an error page and post a message back to the opener window. Successful callbacks will set cookies with appropriate SameSite and Secure attributes, based on HTTPS conditions.\n\n\n**Implementing Cookie Configuration**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on cookie configuration within the callback process. I\'ll implement `secure: true` for HTTPS environments and `sameSite: \'lax\'`, `secure: false` for local HTTP development. Also, I\'m working on returning a clean HTML page with a script that posts a success message back to the opener window and closes, or redirects to `/` if no opener.\nI\'m also working on creating an API endpoint `GET /api/v1/auth/` as a starting point. I\'m moving toward the OAuth Debug panel on the dashboard.\n\n\n**Developing Diagnostic Endpoint**\n\nI\'m currently creating a `/api/v1/auth/` endpoint. It returns diagnostic telemetry, including `googleClientIdConfigured`, `redisStatus`, `databaseStatus`, and other safe metrics. The endpoint checks configurations like Google Client ID and ensures no secrets are leaked. I\'m also ensuring the detection of the runtime fallback redirect URI.\n\n\n\n"
