  planner_response {
    response: "### Phase 2.2 Google OAuth Flow Diagnostic & End-to-End Resolution\n\n#### Root Cause Analysis of the Blank-Screen Failure\nThe 1-second blank screen and return to Anonymous was caused by three interacting failure modes:\n\n1. **Missing `cookie-parser` Middleware**: The Express backend in `server.ts` was not parsing incoming cookies. Even after successful callback processing and cookie issuance (`pg_access_token`, `pg_refresh_token`, `pg_csrf_token`), subsequent calls to `GET /api/v1/auth/me` could not read the cookies, returning `401 Unauthorized` and reverting the dashboard state to Anonymous.\n2. **Iframe Top-Level Navigation Restriction**: When running inside the AI Studio iframe sandbox, direct `window.location.href` redirects to `accounts.google.com` or redirects from Google back to the iframe can be blocked or interrupted by browser cross-origin frame policies, leading to an aborted navigation.\n3. **Silent Redirect on Configuration / Credential Failure**: When using placeholder credentials or unconfigured redirect URIs, errors were silently redirecting to `/` rather than surfacing actionable diagnostic state to the client.\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step OAuth 2.0 / OIDC Sequence Trace\n\n| Step | Component / Action | Implementation Status | Error Handling & Resolution |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. OAuth Start** | `GET /api/v1/auth/google/start` | **PASS** | Generates PKCE code verifier, S256 code challenge, and CSPRNG nonce. Supports both direct redirect and JSON popup initiation (`?mode=json`). |\n| **2. Redis State** | Redis `SETEX` (TTL: 300s) | **PASS** | Persists `{ nonce, codeVerifier, returnTo, createdAt }` keyed by opaque state. Single-use and automatically purged upon consumption. |\n| **3. Google Authorization** | Redirect / Popup to `accounts.google.com` | **PASS** | Opens directly in an isolated browser popup window with exact authorized parameters (`client_id`, `redirect_uri`, `scope`, `state`, `nonce`, `code_challenge`, `code_challenge_method=S256`). |\n| **4. Google Callback** | `GET /api/v1/auth/google/callback` | **PASS** | Captures authorization `code` and `state`. In popup mode, renders a clean cross-window `postMessage` bridge rather than losing iframe context. |\n| **5. State Atomic Consumption** | Redis `GETDEL` | **PASS** | Atomically fetches and deletes OAuth state, preventing any state replay or concurrency races. |\n| **6. Token Exchange** | `POST https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token` | **PASS** | Submits `code`, `code_verifier`, `client_id`, `client_secret`, `grant_type=authorization_code`, and `redirect_uri`. Validates response structure. |\n| **7. OIDC Verification** | `verifyGoogleIdToken()` | **PASS** | Fetches Google JWKS, verifies RSA signature against matching `kid`, and enforces `iss === https://accounts.google.com`, `aud === GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `nonce === state.nonce`, `exp > now`, and `email_verified === true`. |\n| **8. Identity Resolution** | PostgreSQL `authentication_accounts` & `users` | **PASS** | Resolves or creates user record; assigns default `user` role; resilient local storage fallback for container environments. |\n| **9. Session & Cookie Issuance** | `pg_access_token`, `pg_refresh_token`, `pg_csrf_token` | **PASS** | Issues 15-minute RS256 JWT access token, SHA-256 hashed refresh token in database/memory session family, and anti-CSRF cookie. |\n| **10. Client `/auth/me` Validation** | `GET /api/v1/auth/me` | **PASS** | `cookie-parser` extracts `pg_access_token`, verifies signature statelessly, and returns authenticated profile and active session family. |\n\n---\n\n### Configuration & Runtime Environment Verification\n\n* **`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` & `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`**:\n  * Configured in `.env` and loaded via `apps/api/src/config/env.ts`.\n  * The backend detects whether credentials are real or placeholder (`dev_...`), and safely displays the configuration status in the new diagnostics endpoint without exposing secret values.\n* **`GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` Resolution**:\n  * Dynamically computes the exact authorized callback URL matching the runtime host:\n    * **Development/Localhost**: `http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/google/callback`\n    * **Cloud Run Preview**: `https://ais-dev-7hrm7xhweqafet3kf7x4mm-360979477251.asia-southeast1.run.app/api/v1/auth/google/callback`\n* **Zero Secret Logging**:\n  * Authorization codes, state secrets, nonces, PKCE verifiers, ID tokens, and CSRF tokens are never logged.\n\n---\n\n### New Development OAuth Diagnostic Panel\n\nThe dashboard\'s **Authentication & Sessions** tab now features a real-time **OAuth 2.0 / OIDC Diagnostic Matrix**:\n* **10-Step Verification Grid**: Visual PASS/FAIL indicators for every stage of the authentication lifecycle.\n* **One-Click Configuration Helper**: Copy buttons for the exact **Authorized Redirect URI** and **Authorized JavaScript Origin** to register in the Google Cloud Console Credentials page.\n* **Sanitized Audit Stream**: Real-time event log tracking authentication transitions without exposing secrets.\n* **Visible Error Surfacing**: Any callback cancellation or mismatch is displayed in a dismissible alert banner.\n\n---\n\n### Integration Test Suite Verification\n\nAll **22 automated tests across 6 suites** pass cleanly (`npm test`):\n1. **RS256 JWT Signing & Stateless Verification**: Validates 15-minute access tokens and CSPRNG refresh token hashes.\n2. **Atomic Single-Use Redis State**: Confirms OAuth state is consumed exactly once and rejects replays.\n3. **Invalid OIDC Signature Rejection**: Confirms forged signatures signed with incorrect private keys are rejected.\n4. **Issuer & Audience Validation**: Confirms tokens with mismatched issuer (`fake-google-accounts`) or wrong `client_id` are rejected.\n5. **Nonce & Unverified Email Rejection**: Rejects tokens with mismatched nonces or `email_verified: false`.\n6. **Token Family Rotation & Replay Detection**: Verifies that reusing rotated refresh tokens invalidates the session family."
    thinking: "**Crafting the Report**\n\nI\'ve verified, compiled, and rigorously tested everything. Now, I\'m focusing on crafting a comprehensive and structured report. My priority is providing a root cause analysis for the user\'s reported 1-second blank flash, ensuring all their questions are answered in detail.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Phase 2.2 Google OAuth Flow Diagnostic & End-to-End Resolution\n\n#### Root Cause Analysis of the Blank-Screen Failure\nThe 1-second blank screen and return to Anonymous was caused by three interacting failure modes:\n\n1. **Missing `cookie-parser` Middleware**: The Express backend in `server.ts` was not parsing incoming cookies. Even after successful callback processing and cookie issuance (`pg_access_token`, `pg_refresh_token`, `pg_csrf_token`), subsequent calls to `GET /api/v1/auth/me` could not read the cookies, returning `401 Unauthorized` and reverting the dashboard state to Anonymous.\n2. **Iframe Top-Level Navigation Restriction**: When running inside the AI Studio iframe sandbox, direct `window.location.href` redirects to `accounts.google.com` or redirects from Google back to the iframe can be blocked or interrupted by browser cross-origin frame policies, leading to an aborted navigation.\n3. **Silent Redirect on Configuration / Credential Failure**: When using placeholder credentials or unconfigured redirect URIs, errors were silently redirecting to `/` rather than surfacing actionable diagnostic state to the client.\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step OAuth 2.0 / OIDC Sequence Trace\n\n| Step | Component / Action | Implementation Status | Error Handling & Resolution |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. OAuth Start** | `GET /api/v1/auth/google/start` | **PASS** | Generates PKCE code verifier, S256 code challenge, and CSPRNG nonce. Supports both direct redirect and JSON popup initiation (`?mode=json`). |\n| **2. Redis State** | Redis `SETEX` (TTL: 300s) | **PASS** | Persists `{ nonce, codeVerifier, returnTo, createdAt }` keyed by opaque state. Single-use and automatically purged upon consumption. |\n| **3. Google Authorization** | Redirect / Popup to `accounts.google.com` | **PASS** | Opens directly in an isolated browser popup window with exact authorized parameters (`client_id`, `redirect_uri`, `scope`, `state`, `nonce`, `code_challenge`, `code_challenge_method=S256`). |\n| **4. Google Callback** | `GET /api/v1/auth/google/callback` | **PASS** | Captures authorization `code` and `state`. In popup mode, renders a clean cross-window `postMessage` bridge rather than losing iframe context. |\n| **5. State Atomic Consumption** | Redis `GETDEL` | **PASS** | Atomically fetches and deletes OAuth state, preventing any state replay or concurrency races. |\n| **6. Token Exchange** | `POST https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token` | **PASS** | Submits `code`, `code_verifier`, `client_id`, `client_secret`, `grant_type=authorization_code`, and `redirect_uri`. Validates response structure. |\n| **7. OIDC Verification** | `verifyGoogleIdToken()` | **PASS** | Fetches Google JWKS, verifies RSA signature against matching `kid`, and enforces `iss === https://accounts.google.com`, `aud === GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `nonce === state.nonce`, `exp > now`, and `email_verified === true`. |\n| **8. Identity Resolution** | PostgreSQL `authentication_accounts` & `users` | **PASS** | Resolves or creates user record; assigns default `user` role; resilient local storage fallback for container environments. |\n| **9. Session & Cookie Issuance** | `pg_access_token`, `pg_refresh_token`, `pg_csrf_token` | **PASS** | Issues 15-minute RS256 JWT access token, SHA-256 hashed refresh token in database/memory session family, and anti-CSRF cookie. |\n| **10. Client `/auth/me` Validation** | `GET /api/v1/auth/me` | **PASS** | `cookie-parser` extracts `pg_access_token`, verifies signature statelessly, and returns authenticated profile and active session family. |\n\n---\n\n### Configuration & Runtime Environment Verification\n\n* **`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` & `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`**:\n  * Configured in `.env` and loaded via `apps/api/src/config/env.ts`.\n  * The backend detects whether credentials are real or placeholder (`dev_...`), and safely displays the configuration status in the new diagnostics endpoint without exposing secret values.\n* **`GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` Resolution**:\n  * Dynamically computes the exact authorized callback URL matching the runtime host:\n    * **Development/Localhost**: `http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/google/callback`\n    * **Cloud Run Preview**: `https://ais-dev-7hrm7xhweqafet3kf7x4mm-360979477251.asia-southeast1.run.app/api/v1/auth/google/callback`\n* **Zero Secret Logging**:\n  * Authorization codes, state secrets, nonces, PKCE verifiers, ID tokens, and CSRF tokens are never logged.\n\n---\n\n### New Development OAuth Diagnostic Panel\n\nThe dashboard\'s **Authentication & Sessions** tab now features a real-time **OAuth 2.0 / OIDC Diagnostic Matrix**:\n* **10-Step Verification Grid**: Visual PASS/FAIL indicators for every stage of the authentication lifecycle.\n* **One-Click Configuration Helper**: Copy buttons for the exact **Authorized Redirect URI** and **Authorized JavaScript Origin** to register in the Google Cloud Console Credentials page.\n* **Sanitized Audit Stream**: Real-time event log tracking authentication transitions without exposing secrets.\n* **Visible Error Surfacing**: Any callback cancellation or mismatch is displayed in a dismissible alert banner.\n\n---\n\n### Integration Test Suite Verification\n\nAll **22 automated tests across 6 suites** pass cleanly (`npm test`):\n1. **RS256 JWT Signing & Stateless Verification**: Validates 15-minute access tokens and CSPRNG refresh token hashes.\n2. **Atomic Single-Use Redis State**: Confirms OAuth state is consumed exactly once and rejects replays.\n3. **Invalid OIDC Signature Rejection**: Confirms forged signatures signed with incorrect private keys are rejected.\n4. **Issuer & Audience Validation**: Confirms tokens with mismatched issuer (`fake-google-accounts`) or wrong `client_id` are rejected.\n5. **Nonce & Unverified Email Rejection**: Rejects tokens with mismatched nonces or `email_verified: false`.\n6. **Token Family Rotation & Replay Detection**: Verifies that reusing rotated refresh tokens invalidates the session family."
