  planner_response {
    response: "### Security & Configuration Audit Report: Phase 2.2 Google OAuth Implementation\n\n---\n\n### A. Google Credential Status\n\n* **`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`**: **`PLACEHOLDER`** (Configured with default development placeholder: `dev_google_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com`)\n* **`GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`**: **`PLACEHOLDER`** (Configured with default development placeholder: `dev_google_client_secret`)\n* **`GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI`**:\n  * Configured setting: `http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/google/callback`\n  * Dynamic fallback: Resolves dynamically from incoming request protocol and host (`/api/v1/auth/google/callback`) when not explicitly bound to a custom domain.\n* **Credential Exposure & Hardcoding Check**: Verified. No real credentials exist, are stored in memory, or are committed anywhere in the repository.\n\n---\n\n### B. Authoritative Persistence & Fail-Closed Architecture\n\n* **In-Memory Fallbacks Purged**: All `memoryDb` fallback objects and functions have been removed from `apps/api/src/services/auth.service.ts`.\n* **Authoritative Store**: PostgreSQL (`getDatabasePool()`) is strictly authoritative for identity resolution, user creation, session tracking, and token rotation histories.\n* **Fail-Closed Behavior**: If PostgreSQL is unavailable or an error occurs during identity resolution or session insertion, transactions immediately rollback and throw a `DATABASE_UNAVAILABLE` error. No ghost or in-memory fallback sessions are ever issued.\n\n---\n\n### C. `postMessage` Cross-Window Security\n\n* **Strict Origin Targeting**: All server-generated OAuth callback bridge pages now send messages using explicit runtime origins (`${proto}://${host}`) rather than wildcard (`\'*\'`) targets.\n* **Client-Side Origin & Source Verification**: The dashboard listener in `src/App.tsx` enforces:\n  1. `event.origin === window.location.origin`\n  2. `event.source === authPopupRef.current`\n  3. No credentials or JWT tokens are transmitted over `postMessage`; the message is purely a signaling trigger (`OAUTH_AUTH_SUCCESS` / `OAUTH_AUTH_ERROR`) while tokens remain in `HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` cookies.\n\n---\n\n### D. OAuth Failure & Error Handling\n\n* **Explicit Error Boundary**: When Google OAuth authorization fails or is cancelled by the user:\n  * An explicit error view is rendered with the sanitized error code.\n  * The error status is posted back to the parent dashboard window.\n  * Diagnostics record the failure step.\n  * The user is never silently redirected to the anonymous dashboard.\n* **State Replay Protection**: OAuth transactions stored in Redis (300s TTL) are consumed via atomic `GETDEL`. Replayed or expired state tokens fail closed.\n\n---\n\n### E. Development vs. Production Separation\n\n* **Safe Diagnostics**: `/api/v1/auth/diagnostics` is restricted to development mode and returns `403 Forbidden` if `NODE_ENV === \'production\'`.\n* **Clean Redirect Lists**: Hardcoded cloud preview URLs have been removed; redirect URIs dynamically adapt or bind to the canonical production environment variable.\n\n---\n\n### F. Verification & Build Results\n\n#### 1. Automated Test Suite (`npm test`)\n```text\n\342\234\224 RS256 JWT Token Service Tests (2 tests)\n\342\234\224 RBAC & Privilege Boundary Tests (1 test)\n\342\234\224 Environment Configuration (1 test)\n\342\234\224 Health Endpoints Integration (1 test)\n\342\234\224 OAuth Failure Cases & Diagnostics Matrix Tests (10 tests)\n\342\234\224 OIDC ID Token Validation Unit Tests (7 tests)\n\nTotal: 22 passed, 0 failed, 6 suites\nExecution Time: ~3.5s\n```\n\n#### 2. Production Build (`npm run build`)\n```text\n\342\234\223 1673 modules transformed.\ndist/index.html                   0.77 kB \342\224\202 gzip:   0.36 kB\ndist/assets/index-CwMurcn9.css   27.03 kB \342\224\202 gzip:   5.60 kB\ndist/assets/index-CTjL19Xs.js   451.41 kB \342\224\202 gzip: 128.11 kB\ndist/server.cjs                  64.20 kB \342\224\202 dist/server.cjs.map: 111.20 kB\n\342\234\223 Build completed successfully with 0 errors.\n```\n\n---\n\n### G. Steps Required to Enable Real Google Sign-In\n\nTo complete Google OAuth authentication with live credentials:\n1. Create a project in the **Google Cloud Console**.\n2. Create an **OAuth 2.0 Client ID** (Web application).\n3. Add your deployment\'s callback URL (e.g., `https://<YOUR_DOMAIN>/api/v1/auth/google/callback`) to **Authorized redirect URIs**.\n4. Set the environment variables in `.env`:\n   ```env\n   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com\n   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret\n   GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://<YOUR_DOMAIN>/api/v1/auth/google/callback\n   ```"
